This study's primary objective is to provide evidence for the existence of stationary solutions in deterministic equations inspired by the Kardar-Parisi-Zhang (KPZ) type, which incorporate non-local terms that are dependent on the gradient of the solution. A specific example is the equation
\begin{equation*}
  \partial_t h = \Delta^2 h + \nabla \cdot [h \partial_n \Delta h] + \nabla \cdot [(\nabla h)^2 \partial_n h].
  \end{equation*}
  It is worth noting that the latter term is the primary contributor to the complexity of the problem as it introduces a significant challenge to the use of standard comparison principle tools.
